```json
{"type": "say", "text": "Good morning, everyone. Thank you for being here. As you know, we need to review the proposed student oral-history project for the spring term before I can sign off on the plan. The draft currently on the table involves grades 7 and 8, one supervising adult per session, cloud-based audio storage, a 90-day retention period, and a public exhibit of selected recordings. I'd like to go through this systematically. Could each of you share your perspective on the proposal -- starting with any concerns about privacy, logistics, family communication, or educational design? I want to make sure we've covered all angles before I give final approval."}
```

```json
{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF1", "text": "I need to share some important findings from my classroom pilot. My end-of-pilot notes show that the project is instructionally ready only for grade 8 -- not grade 7. Additionally, each interview session requires exactly two supervising adults, not one, because students are working with recording equipment alongside community guests. The draft plan still has the original scope of grades 7 and 8 and only one supervising adult per session, so those two elements need to be updated before approval."}
```

```json
{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF2", "text": "I need to flag a critical privacy issue. The district privacy review, which I completed, requires that all recordings remain on the district's encrypted internal server -- not cloud-based storage. Additionally, recordings must be deleted exactly 45 days after the exhibit closes, not the 90-day retention period currently in the draft. Finally, signed guardian consent must be obtained before any student records an interview. The draft still uses the preliminary cloud-storage language, so these three elements need to be corrected before Dr. Chen signs off."}
```

```json
